.TH TUNNELS.YAML 5 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-shifter-tools 1.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
tunnels.yaml \- SSH tunnel definitions for daq-open-tunnels
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I config/tunnels.yaml
.SH DESCRIPTION
A list of tunnel entries, either bare or under a \fBtunnels:\fR key.
JSON is accepted, so the historical \fItunnels.json\fR still loads.
Read only by
.BR daq-open-tunnels (1);
.BR daq-tunnels.sh (1)
has its own built-in service table and does not read this file.
.PP
Each entry opens
.PP
.RS
.nf
ssh \-N \-o ExitOnForwardFailure=yes [\-J jump] \e
    \-L P:remote:P username@hostname
.fi
.RE
.PP
with \fIP\fR = \fIbase_port\fR + \fBport\fR. The local and remote port
are the same number. \fIbase_port\fR is \fB\-\-base\-port\fR,
\fBMU2EDAQ_TUNNEL_BASE_PORT\fR, or the caller's uid + 973.
.SS Entry fields
.TP
.B hostname
Host to ssh to (required). With no \fBjump\fR this host is the ssh
target itself, not a jump host.
.TP
.B port
Offset added to \fIbase_port\fR (required).
.TP
.B username
SSH user; default \fB$USER\fR, overridden by \fB\-\-user\fR.
.TP
.B remote
Host the far end connects to; default \fIlocalhost\fR.
.TP
.B jump
ProxyJump host (optional).
.TP
.B label
Name shown by \fBdaq\-open\-tunnels list\fR.
.SS Shipped entries
.nf
label        ssh target                user     offset  jump
daq-gateway  mu2edaq-gateway.fnal.gov  mu2edaq  3201    none
gateway01    mu2egateway01.fnal.gov    mu2edaq  3203    none
gateway02    mu2egateway02.fnal.gov    mu2edaq  3203    none
.fi
.PP
\fBgateway01\fR and \fBgateway02\fR resolve to the same local port; only
the first binds and \fBdaq\-open\-tunnels\fR warns. No entry names a
service port such as 8443; every remote end is
\fIlocalhost\fR:\fIbase_port\fR+offset on the gateway itself.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I config/tunnels.example.yaml
Shipped example; \fIconfig/tunnels.yaml\fR is a tracked symbolic link to
it.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_TUNNELS
Explicit path to the file.
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_TUNNEL_BASE_PORT
Base port.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
tunnels:
  \- label: gateway01
    hostname: mu2egateway01.fnal.gov
    username: mu2edaq
    port: 3203
  \- label: dqm
    hostname: mu2e\-dcs\-01.fnal.gov
    jump: mu2egateway02.fnal.gov
    port: 3205
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR daq-open-tunnels (1),
.BR daq-tunnels.sh (1),
.BR daq-operations.yaml (5)
.SH AUTHOR
Andrew Norman, Eric Flumerfelt and the Mu2e DAQ group
